#X obj 694 8 window;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 255 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Computes the value of a window function at a given index
\, or outputs all window values at once. The window type and size are
set by the TYPE and SIZE arguments or by the @type and @size properties.;
#X text 240 153 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 178 • Windowing for spectral analysis — preparing data
for FFT by multiplying the signal with a window shape (Hann \, Hamming
\, Blackman \, etc.) \, so that spectral leakage is reduced.;
#X text 250 248 • Envelope shapes and fades — using the output of the
object as a smooth amplitude envelope (for example \, for grain windows
in a granulator \, crossfades or micro-fades).;
